  "summary": "Broad codex-vs-implementation audit after rev 190: (a) seven active principles still prescribe Python roles (P115 role map, P18/P23 stack lists, P118 post-reduction lane, P119 Windows bridge hop, P120 Python-default routing, P121 Python fallback chain) contradicting B166/B73/B34 total retirement; (b) git_worktree_registry points four worktrees at the nonexistent E:\\GPTBridge-worktrees\\ root and omits the devin worktree, while metadata.git_persistent_worktree_pool carries one stale duplicate and one brace-list missing devin; (c) project_architecture_directory keeps QDRANT_AUTHORITY active although every qdrant schema object is retired and vectord-rs is the canonical store, RAG_HYBRID points at the deleted main-system\\src-core\\core_system\\rag path (RAG lives at Standalone tools/ragd-rs), MODEL_DIALOGUE points at local-model\\model-dialogue while the tool manifest declares Standalone tools\\model-dialogue, STAR_DIRECTORY retirement is already handled by the in-flight star-directory-retire-2026-09-18-r3 request (not re-proposed here), and eight registered implementation components (vectord, searchd-go, julia-compute, business-logic-fsharp, star-chat, resource-governor, model-training-native, local-vector) have no architecture-directory row; (d) rag_contract_registry still names QDRANT as canonical authority; (e) implementation_obligations reference retired TypeScript/Python wording; (f) final_implementation_inventory current rows describe five worktrees and a hybrid Python implementation. All changes converge codex registries/text to registered implementation reality; no implementation is modified.",
